\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Speaker output stage. The PWM signal from the FPGA is buffered by a unity inverting op amp (configured with equal resistors so gain is $-1$, polarity is then absorbed into the PWM table), then low pass filtered by an RC stage tuned to roll off above the audible band, then fed to the small 8 ohm speaker.}}{17}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
